# The image build consumes the Go module under server/ plus the web
# app's build inputs (web/ sources, the shared i18n/ table at the
# repository root, and the generated TypeScript contract types); every
# other repository path (git history, docs, generated mobile clients,
# tooling state) stays out of the build context so that context
# transfers stay small and layer cache invalidation tracks the server
# and web sources alone. The trailing exclusions keep build output and
# dependency trees out of the re-included paths: the image builds the
# web app itself in its own stage, so host build output must never
# ride into the context.
**
!server/**
!web/**
!i18n/**
!openapi/generated/web/**
web/node_modules
web/build
web/.svelte-kit
web/e2e/.auth
web/test-results
server/internal/web/dist
